runtime: forward non-terminal input through public SSH

The public launcher discarded stdin before calling the existing SSH
transport, so piped resource scripts reached the remote command as EOF.
Pass non-terminal stdin directly through the existing input seam while
holding the same gate. Terminal invocations continue to send no input.

Cover exact piped/file bytes, empty EOF and the terminal no-read branch
through the real transport with an owned synthetic SSH executable. Keep
strict trust, environment clearing and remote argument handling unchanged.
